def bubble_sort(nums):
    n = len(nums)
    for i in range(n):
        swapped = False
        for j in range(0, n - i - 1):
            if nums[j] > nums[j + 1]:
                nums[j], nums[j + 1] = nums[j + 1], nums[j]
                swapped = True
        if not swapped:
            break
    return nums
```

This corrected implementation of the bubble sort algorithm includes a flag `swapped` to track whether any swaps were made in the inner loop. If no swaps were made, it means the list is already sorted, and we can break out of the outer loop early, reducing the time complexity to O(n^2) in the worst case.

